lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Popular Repository&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cderv/r-bucket&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;r-bucket&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;66 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;6&lt;br&gt;Personal scoop bucket I use as an R user and software engineer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Other Repositories (Pinned)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-cli&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;quarto-cli&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;6.2k &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;494&lt;br&gt;Open-source scientific and technical publishing system built on Pandoc.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/quarto-dev/q2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;q2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;320 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;23&lt;br&gt;q2 is the experimental implementation of Quarto 2 in Rust.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/rstudio/rmarkdown&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;rmarkdown&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;3.1k &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;990&lt;br&gt;Dynamic Documents for R&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-r&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;quarto-r&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;160 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;29&lt;br&gt;R interface to quarto-cli&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cscheid/braid&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;braid&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;16 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;3&lt;br&gt;An automerge-centric issue tracker for LLM agents&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;I&#39;m on the Quarto team at Posit. Quarto is an open-source system for publishing scientific and technical documents. I work mostly on &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-cli&quot;&gt;quarto-cli&lt;/a&gt; and contribute to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/quarto-dev/q2&quot;&gt;the next version&lt;/a&gt;, a rewrite in Rust.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I also maintain the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-r&quot;&gt;quarto R package&lt;/a&gt; and several R Markdown packages, such as &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/rstudio/rticles&quot;&gt;rticles&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/rstudio/distill&quot;&gt;distill&lt;/a&gt;. With Yihui Xie and Emily Riederer, I co-wrote the &lt;a href=&quot;https://pkg.yihui.org/rmarkdown-cookbook/&quot;&gt;R Markdown Cookbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I do most of my coding with AI agents, on Windows. When one of those tools breaks on Windows, I open an issue or send a fix.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Happy to talk about Quarto, scientific publishing or coding with agents on Windows. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/cderv&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; is the best place to reach me.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cderv/cderv/main/profile/stats.svg?sanitize=true&quot; alt=&quot;GitHub stats for cderv&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
